  "id": "love-withdrawal",
  "term": "love withdrawal",
  "definition": "Love withdrawal is a form of parental psychological control in which affection becomes conditional on a child’s obedience or meeting expectations. It can lead children to link being loved with compliance, increasing fear of rejection and disrupting healthy emotional and empathic development.",
